{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '34384,34408p' src/ontology/cl-edit.owl\"","aggregated_output":"\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31183831\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31613440\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052022 \"A smooth muscle cell that is part of the fallopian tube. This cell is responsible for peristaltic contractions that facilitate gamete and embryo transport, fluid mixing, and embryo admission to the uterus.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4052022 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4052022 \"2024-10-21T12:16:54Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31613440\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4052022 \"oviduct smooth muscle cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31613440\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4052022 \"uterine tube smooth muscle cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18621753\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4052022 \"The fallopian tube smooth muscle cell in the human contracts dynamically in response to hormones and signaling molecules. Prostaglandins, particularly PGF2α and PGE2, have been shown to increase muscular contractions, while progesterone, levonorgestrel, mifepristone, oxytocin, and human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG) decrease them. These contractile responses are crucial for regulating gamete and embryo transport through the fallopian tube.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4052022 \"fallopian tube smooth muscle cell\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4052022 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000192 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0003889)))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_4052023 (luminal endometrial unciliated epithelial cell)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32929266\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36581776\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38559249\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39198675\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052023 \"An epithelial cell that is part of the endometrial luminal epithelium, forming a continuous layer lining the uterine cavity. This cell undergoes cyclical changes during the menstrual cycle, proliferating under estrogen in the proliferative phase, and differentiating under progesterone in the secretory phase to prepare for potential implantation. During the window of implantation, this cell changes from a tall columnar shape to a shorter columnar or cuboidal form, loses polarity, and becomes receptive to blastocyst implantation.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4052023 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4052023 \"2024-10-22T12:02:23Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39198675\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4052023 \"The luminal endometrial unciliated epithelial cell expresses WNT7A, and LGR5 during the proliferative phase, transitioning to express VTCN1 and SULT1E1 in the early secretory phase, and LEFTY1, IL6, and PTGS1 in the mid- to late-secretory phases.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4052023 \"luminal endometrial unciliated epithelial cell\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4052023 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000066 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0011949) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0032940)))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_4052024 (myotendinous junction nucleus)\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33311457\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33311464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38398025\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052024 \"A specialized muscle nucleus that is part of an extrafusal muscle fiber and overlaps the muscle-tendon junction, where muscle fibers connect to tendons. Characterized by a distinct transcriptional profile with the expression of genes like COL22A1, this myonucleus supports the structural integrity and function of the junction, playing a key role in transmitting the force generated by muscle contraction to the tendon.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4052024 <https://orcid.org/0009-0000-8480-9277>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4052024 <https://orcid.org/0009-0001-6947-615X>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4052024 \"2024-10-30T13:47:39Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
